"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nI really enjoyed reading this.  \nI'm not a fast reader, but I finished this thick book in no time.  \n\nThe collapse of basic physics as we know it and the resulting suicides of scientists in the early part of the book, along with stories jumping between the past and present and a mysterious virtual game world... these elements are scattered at first.  \nUp to that point, I couldn't tell what the main story was.  \n\nHowever, as I reached the middle, everything started to connect.  \nThe concept of the Three-body problem was particularly impressive.  \n\nI was so curious about what happens next that I immediately started the next book in the series.  \n"